      "description": "They’re worlds apart—or so it seems. But sports and computing have one thing in common: the constant pursuit of speed and progress. The Mainboard superfamily is our approach to expressing these ambitions typographically. Mainboard Mono has been developed from a sleek, spurless sans with on-screen usage in mind. Generous apertures and rectangular dots ensure easy legibility in all resolutions. The family of 7 weights comes with 500+ glyphs. You can fine-tune it by toggling various stylistic sets and figure sets. Pair it with its proportional sibling, Mainboard: this winning combination might just give you the edge over those runner-ups breathing down your neck while you’re coding the future.",
